cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software or its SF-SJ planning scenario, please cite this repository."
title: "Bay Area UAM Link-Quality Simulator"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Zhang
    given-names: Ziyi
abstract: >-
  A reproducible toolkit for a Caltrain-referenced San Francisco to San Jose UAM
  corridor: the 75.423 km centerline, 18 retained physical macro-site locations,
  a deterministic RSRP/SINR link-quality kernel based on the 3GPP TR 36.777
  UMa-AV LOS path-loss model, a single-UAM multi-rate simulator with an
  interactive 2D/3D dashboard, and multi-UAM motion control: policy-dependent
  longitudinal spacing (ACC and AKS), lane-change profiles checked against a coupled
  acceleration envelope and NMAC, a Bay Area policy calibration, and a 3 x 3 corridor
  capacity experiment. Parts of the code, tests, and documentation were
  developed with AI coding assistants (OpenAI Codex and Anthropic Claude),
  limited to implementation, refactoring, test authoring, and drafting; the
  scenario definition, site selection and evidence review, modeling assumptions,
  and interpretation of results are the author's own.
version: 0.2.0
date-released: 2026-09-14
license:
